Solutions: x = 3.0, x = 2.0
```

## JavaScript code

```javascript
const fibonacci = (n) => {
  if (n <= 1) return n;
  return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
};

console.log(fibonacci(10)); // 55
```

This version runs in exponential time. A memoized version is much faster for larger `n`:

```javascript
const fibMemo = (n, memo = new Map()) => {
  if (n <= 1) return n;
  if (memo.has(n)) return memo.get(n);
  const value = fibMemo(n - 1, memo) + fibMemo(n - 2, memo);
  memo.set(n, value);
  return value;
};

console.log(fibMemo(50)); // 12586269025
```

